1
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:30,810
I am

2
00:00:30,893 --> 00:00:31,723
not sure

3
00:00:31,806 --> 00:00:33,157
how to forget that

4
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:37,460
I am But I am not sure how much I am

5
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:44,540
What can you say to this sky?

6
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:52,020
But what can you say to this day?
I am not sure how to understand

7
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:19,680
Oh, my love.

8
00:01:34,740 --> 00:01:38,460
So we got into this amazing
battle against Venom Myotismon.

9
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:42,160
Raymon and Garurumon digivolved
to Mega for the first time.

10
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:44,900
But even that couldn't stop him. Finally,

11
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:50,057
we combined all our powers and that totally
blasted Venom Myotismon into Digidust.

12
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:53,100
Afterwards, the digital
world appeared in the sky.

13
00:01:53,460 --> 00:01:56,457
What Izzy figured is that while
we've been back here on Earth,

14
00:01:56,540 --> 00:01:58,917
things have gotten much
worse on the other side.

15
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:01,657
So now we're going back
to fix the problems there.

16
00:02:01,740 --> 00:02:04,237
It was a bummer to have to
leave our parents so soon,

17
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:06,732
but saving two worlds is kinda important.

18
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:12,500
Mano Yama no Shitenu, Dark Masters.

19
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:22,905
Those fit players are
frozen with stage fright,

20
00:02:23,220 --> 00:02:25,917
hopelessly waiting for the
moment they'll be saved.

21
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,960
And yet there's an
unseen twist in the plot.

22
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:32,788
I say we cut to the punchline
and go straight for the action.

23
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:36,621
Oh, please, that would be boring.

24
00:02:37,340 --> 00:02:39,580
I want to play this drama to the hilt.

25
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:43,617
Let's pull out all the staffs
and give them what they paid for.

26
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:45,229
I'm in complete agreement.

27
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:47,257
A quick victory would be let down.

28
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:49,957
The Digidestined will be
on Spiral Mountain soon.

29
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:51,897
We must rehearse before they get here.

30
00:02:51,980 --> 00:02:54,140
It will be their final performance!

31
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:01,560
Metal Sea Deramon, Puppet
Mon, and Machine Deramon.

32
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:04,741
I present to you the
downfall of the Digidestined!

33
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:25,017
Well, it looks like we're back.

34
00:03:25,100 --> 00:03:25,930
Back where?

35
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:27,277
In the digital world?

36
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:28,478
That's affirmative.

37
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:29,920
It's dark.

38
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:31,631
Yeah, it's kind of weird.

39
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:34,480
Hey, look up there!

40
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:38,180
Talk about weird.

41
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:39,860
Could that be Earth?

42
00:03:40,480 --> 00:03:44,377
It's merely speculation, but it
seems to be a reasonable facsimile.

43
00:03:44,460 --> 00:03:48,284
We see Earth from here, like we
saw the digital world from Earth.

44
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:49,510
Huh?

45
00:03:49,740 --> 00:03:50,570
Gomamon.

46
00:03:50,653 --> 00:03:51,518
Hey, where are you?

47
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:56,040
Jo, I've been snoozing over here. Huh?

48
00:03:56,980 --> 00:03:59,745
Oh, we'll just save the
world without you then.

49
00:04:00,260 --> 00:04:01,090
Jo!

50
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:02,640
Oh, I didn't need this.

51
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:05,200
Koromon, Digiball, too! Agumon!

52
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:06,637
Tanemon, Digiball, too!

53
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:07,550
Babubon!

54
00:04:07,633 --> 00:04:09,357
Musumon, Digiball, too! Dunjumon!

55
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:10,617
Nucumon, Digiball, too!

56
00:04:10,700 --> 00:04:11,530
Monamon!

57
00:04:11,613 --> 00:04:13,100
Yokomon, Digiball, too! Biyomon!

58
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:16,600
Hold on! Huh?

59
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:22,300
Come out.

60
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:24,140
You're among friends.

61
00:04:25,660 --> 00:04:27,040
We won't hurt you.

62
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:28,400
Don't be afraid.

63
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:36,220
Oh, my goodness! It's Chuumon!

64
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:37,297
He looks terrible.

65
00:04:37,380 --> 00:04:39,556
What he needs is a complete makeover.

66
00:04:40,660 --> 00:04:42,240
Mimi? Palmon?

67
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:45,140
Something bad happened.

68
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:47,677
Sukamon and Chuumon
used to be inseparable.

69
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:49,936
I'm so glad you came back to save us.

70
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:52,700
Would somebody mind helping me?

71
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:55,024
Whoops, I forgot all about you!

72
00:04:55,860 --> 00:04:57,140
Uh-oh! You forgot.

73
00:04:57,340 --> 00:05:00,177
I'm hanging here by my elbows
and you're off in La La Land!

74
00:05:00,260 --> 00:05:02,848
Gee, I wonder what it's
like to have elbows.

75
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:04,280
Joe! Figures.

76
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:05,670
Huh?

77
00:05:05,753 --> 00:05:07,080
Hey, quit fooling around!

78
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:11,437
Just help me, will you?

79
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:13,000
I'll work with us.

80
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:15,800
What's happening?

81
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:17,472
Everything's gone wacko.

82
00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:25,277
Are you trying to get a hold of Gen-Eye?

83
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:27,242
Well, I'm not playing solitaire.

84
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:28,941
Chumon's a mess.

85
00:05:29,060 --> 00:05:30,377
I wonder what happened to him.

86
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:32,857
Well, whatever it was,
it wasn't very pretty.

87
00:05:32,940 --> 00:05:33,770
Poor thing.

88
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:35,430
Oh.

89
00:05:37,940 --> 00:05:38,980
Chuumon? Mimi.

90
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:42,980
I wasn't dreaming it's really
you after all. Poor thing.

91
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:45,536
Why don't you tell Mimi all about it?

92
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:48,136
What happened to your friend Sukamon?

93
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:49,717
I... I...

94
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:51,760
I'm afraid I lost him.

95
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:59,480
After you guys left Vile Island, Sukamon
and I went on with life as usual.

96
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:02,540
You know, eating, eating, and more eating.

97
00:06:03,820 --> 00:06:04,940
When suddenly...

98
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:13,700
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

99
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:18,060
Oh, oh, oh!

100
00:06:18,740 --> 00:06:19,570
Superman!

101
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:24,420
I never saw him again.

102
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:29,037
A powerful evil force took over the land,
causing all kinds of bad things to happen.

103
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:32,557
Then it rebuilt the digital world,
so it would be easier to conquer.

104
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:34,287
I've been hiding ever since.

105
00:06:35,440 --> 00:06:39,017
You mean the digital world has
completely changed from what it was?

106
00:06:39,100 --> 00:06:40,218
How's it different?

107
00:06:43,460 --> 00:06:45,937
Everything's been
discombobulated and taken apart.

108
00:06:46,020 --> 00:06:48,657
The digital world has been
relocated way up there.

109
00:06:48,740 --> 00:06:50,600
It's called Spiral Mountain.

110
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:57,468
There's nothing left here of
the old world except some ruins.

111
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:59,657
So you're saying it's all up there?

112
00:06:59,740 --> 00:07:03,497
Huh, color me cynical, but nothing
surprises me about this place.

113
00:07:03,580 --> 00:07:05,457
Where did all the other Digimon go?

114
00:07:05,540 --> 00:07:06,370
Are they up there too?

115
00:07:06,453 --> 00:07:08,500
Where's Leomon? I don't know.

116
00:07:09,260 --> 00:07:10,090
But,

117
00:07:10,173 --> 00:07:13,737
from what I've been told, they'll destroy
anything that tries to get in their way.

118
00:07:13,820 --> 00:07:15,200
Who will? Who?

119
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:17,500
The Dark Masters. Well,

120
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:21,197
they couldn't be too much tougher than
anybody else we've wrestled with before.

121
00:07:21,280 --> 00:07:22,110
No way!

122
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:24,577
They'll beat the pants right off of you!

123
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:27,977
We got rid of Myotismon, so
we could get rid of them, too.

124
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:29,295
Don't worry about it.

125
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:33,057
As long as the eight of us are together,
we'll keep those big bullies away from you.

126
00:07:33,140 --> 00:07:33,970
Yeah!

127
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:38,800
I've been waiting for you, Digi-Designy.

128
00:07:40,780 --> 00:07:41,720
Oh, no!

129
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:43,273
It's Metal Sea Tremont!

130
00:07:45,520 --> 00:07:51,460
And this guy is one real hard-nosed,
and I mean hard-nosed. Take my advice.

131
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:54,440
This is one train that
you would rather miss.

132
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:11,089
Okay, if that's the way you
want it, we can play rough, too!

133
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:15,900
Let's go, Agumon! Gotcha!

134
00:08:18,260 --> 00:08:19,731
Agumon, Digiball, please!

135
00:08:21,020 --> 00:08:21,850
Raymon!

136
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:24,120
Now it's our turn!

137
00:08:24,820 --> 00:08:26,240
Gabumon, Digiball, too!

138
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:28,110
Jaruruma!

139
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:30,960
Biamon, Digiball, go!

140
00:08:32,340 --> 00:08:33,400
Bergamon!

141
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,940
Tanjaman, Digiball too!

142
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:38,540
Kabuterimon!

143
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:40,040
Ah-ha-ha!

144
00:08:41,260 --> 00:08:42,920
Stabaman, Digiball too!

145
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,140
Heakakuman!

146
00:08:46,180 --> 00:08:47,800
Balamon, Digiball too!

147
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:49,220
Bergamon!

148
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:52,400
Balamon, Digiball too!

149
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:54,030
Balamon!

150
00:08:54,113 --> 00:08:54,943
Tanjaman!

151
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:57,860
Balamon, Digiball too!

152
00:08:58,300 --> 00:09:00,857
Balamon, Digiball too!

153
00:09:00,940 --> 00:09:02,100
Yeah!

154
00:09:02,780 --> 00:09:04,600
Nova Brat!

155
00:09:08,580 --> 00:09:10,460
Meteor wing!

156
00:09:11,140 --> 00:09:12,860
Howling blaster!

157
00:09:14,940 --> 00:09:16,080
Electro-shocker!

158
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:17,680
Harpoon torpedo!

159
00:09:19,040 --> 00:09:20,660
How about torpedo spray?

160
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:26,260
Lightning paw!

161
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:34,320
Angemon! Oh, no!

162
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:37,502
You should know your powers
aren't strong enough.

163
00:09:38,180 --> 00:09:40,840
How come he's beating us so badly? Ah,

164
00:09:41,180 --> 00:09:45,077
it's because he's a Mega Digimon and even
eight champions can't overtake one Mega.

165
00:09:45,160 --> 00:09:47,395
He's stronger than all of us combined.

166
00:09:47,940 --> 00:09:49,997
Then we're lost without more power.

167
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:53,177
Ever notice we're always at the
wrong place at just the wrong time?

168
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:55,860
Now it's time to take one nasty ride!

169
00:10:00,940 --> 00:10:02,520
Oh! Ah!

170
00:10:03,940 --> 00:10:04,770
Ah!

171
00:10:05,380 --> 00:10:06,210
Ah!

172
00:10:06,980 --> 00:10:07,810
Oh!

173
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:24,940
Oh!

174
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:32,480
T .K., are you all right?

175
00:10:32,860 --> 00:10:35,920
I thought I was broken,
but I guess I must be okay.

176
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:38,670
Huh?

177
00:10:41,060 --> 00:10:42,740
What's the matter? Wait.

178
00:10:43,020 --> 00:10:44,080
I'll be back.

179
00:10:48,900 --> 00:10:49,800
Roger, Mom!

180
00:10:54,060 --> 00:10:55,800
Oh, no! Poor Gatomon!

181
00:11:03,540 --> 00:11:05,800
Be prepared for another Mega Digimon.

182
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:08,169
He's called Machinedramon.

183
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:12,920
This metallic mutant can blow out a
Digimon just like a birthday candle.

184
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:19,217
Digimon! Digimon!
Digimon! Digimon! Digimon!

185
00:11:19,300 --> 00:11:21,300
Digimon! Digimon!

186
00:11:23,300 --> 00:11:24,277
Digimon!

187
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:25,320
Digimon!

188
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:26,540
Bastard!

189
00:11:27,020 --> 00:11:28,000
Digimon!

190
00:11:28,260 --> 00:11:29,320
Digimon, too!

191
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:30,740
Bastard!

192
00:11:31,140 --> 00:11:32,434
I'm not in the jungle!

193
00:11:33,640 --> 00:11:36,000
That's a dream!

194
00:11:40,380 --> 00:11:41,760
Uhuru man!

195
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:43,120
Digimon, too!

196
00:11:49,300 --> 00:11:50,600
Megadramon!

197
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:55,900
Kabuterimon Digimon 2!

198
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:01,520
Mega Kabuterimon!

199
00:12:03,020 --> 00:12:05,860
Perjabon Digimon 2!

200
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,720
Garudamon!

201
00:12:13,300 --> 00:12:14,900
Perjabon Digimon 2!

202
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:19,030
Gwilymon!

203
00:12:23,120 --> 00:12:24,520
Ikkakumon!

204
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:25,980
Digivolve to!

205
00:12:30,100 --> 00:12:31,500
Zoodlemon!

206
00:12:34,300 --> 00:12:35,700
Gatomon!

207
00:12:36,100 --> 00:12:37,360
Digivolve to!

208
00:12:41,320 --> 00:12:42,720
Angewomon!

209
00:12:45,460 --> 00:12:47,977
Come on, guys, show them
what you're made of!

210
00:12:48,060 --> 00:12:50,097
Hope they're made of
something strong enough.

211
00:12:50,180 --> 00:12:51,010
Huh?

212
00:13:06,660 --> 00:13:07,490
Archibulmon!

213
00:13:19,860 --> 00:13:20,700
We stopped.

214
00:13:21,060 --> 00:13:22,060
I can't complain.

215
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:25,202
It's sure a lot better
than falling on our heads.

216
00:13:27,940 --> 00:13:30,317
Hey, can't you two take
a break for one minute?

217
00:13:30,400 --> 00:13:31,230
Yeah, come on.

218
00:13:31,313 --> 00:13:32,937
We're all supposed to be on the same side.

219
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:35,240
We can't control it. That's right.

220
00:13:35,380 --> 00:13:37,897
Our bodies are doing
this all by themselves.

221
00:13:37,980 --> 00:13:39,480
All by themselves, huh?

222
00:13:40,680 --> 00:13:43,209
Oh, I've always hated
any form of exercise.

223
00:13:43,380 --> 00:13:44,210
What's happening to me?

224
00:13:44,293 --> 00:13:48,000
We've become string puppets,
and someone's operating us.

225
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,817
Well, aren't we, little smarty-peak?

226
00:13:50,900 --> 00:13:52,800
Who are you? You want to know?

227
00:13:52,940 --> 00:13:56,457
How about if I help you look up my
profile on your special computer?

228
00:13:56,540 --> 00:13:57,370
Watch.

229
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:04,720
He's also a Mega Digimon.

230
00:14:05,220 --> 00:14:08,357
Puppetmon has a controlling
personality and a rotten temper.

231
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:11,017
Get him mad and he'll
bop you with his hammer.

232
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:12,357
If you have to hit something,

233
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:15,157
you should bop yourself for how
you look in that stupid helmet.

234
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:16,070
Mimi!

235
00:14:16,153 --> 00:14:18,216
I'm gonna have to let you go for now.

236
00:14:19,580 --> 00:14:21,720
I promise to destroy you!

237
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:24,220
Puppet Bravo!

238
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:51,260
Well, hello there, boys
and girls, and welcome.

239
00:14:51,780 --> 00:14:54,600
Today, I'm going to tell
you an amazing story.

240
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:57,837
Once upon a time, there
were eight Digidestined.

241
00:14:57,920 --> 00:15:01,237
They went with their Digimon
companions to try to save the world.

242
00:15:01,320 --> 00:15:04,897
The children and their Digimon discovered
that in order for them to do it,

243
00:15:04,980 --> 00:15:07,857
they had to climb up to
the top of Spiral Mountain.

244
00:15:07,940 --> 00:15:10,617
But to their dismay, the
Dark Masters defeated them.

245
00:15:10,700 --> 00:15:11,530
So sad.

246
00:15:11,613 --> 00:15:14,180
Hey, clowny, nobody's
laughing at your story.

247
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:15,737
Oh, dear, I'm so sorry.

248
00:15:15,820 --> 00:15:17,737
Did I happen to mention the story is true?

249
00:15:17,820 --> 00:15:20,349
I wanted to give you
a preview of the plot.

250
00:15:23,020 --> 00:15:23,850
Fools!

251
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:25,540
Ah, it's Palmon!

252
00:15:26,140 --> 00:15:29,060
He's a Mega Phantom
Digimon of the worst kind.

253
00:15:29,400 --> 00:15:31,697
You never know what he's
gonna look like next.

254
00:15:31,780 --> 00:15:34,427
Well, I think your plot
needs a few rewrites.

255
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:35,670
Agumon!

256
00:15:35,753 --> 00:15:36,933
Gabumon, you can do it!

257
00:15:38,100 --> 00:15:39,560
Agumon, more Digibomb!

258
00:16:00,820 --> 00:16:04,540
Digimon, Digital Monsters,
Digimon are the champions!

259
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:06,800
WarGreymon!

260
00:16:07,400 --> 00:16:09,480
Digital Monsters, Digimon, Digimon!

261
00:16:10,460 --> 00:16:12,520
Gabumon, drop Digiball too!

262
00:16:16,240 --> 00:16:19,760
Digimon, Digimon monsters,
Digimon are the champions!

263
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:29,520
